- **Blank rows below the cursor**: on shrink, Termux first drops the rows below the cursor that hold only spaces (styles are ignored). When those rows sit above non-blank ones, the lines below them are cut off the bottom of the screen. Before, this left a gap (one case lost `line 11`). The model counts those rows the same way, truncates `previousLines` to what is still on screen, and the next frame writes the cut lines again. Two more Termux details are modelled: a cursor pushed above the screen is reset to its first row, and growth pulls rows back from the scrollback.
- **Fallback**: when the rows Termux moves cannot be known, it repaints in full, as before. That covers content that never filled the screen and was not drawn after a clear (rows above it unknown), a scrollback that holds stale or repeated rows after `redrawViewport()`, and a cursor above the screen.
